WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.190
Running a live stream means juggling chat, overlays and alerts,

2
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.969
all at the same time.

3
00:00:06.969 --> 00:00:11.925
Here's how Social Stream Ninja and a Stream Deck make that a lot easier.

4
00:00:12.675 --> 00:00:15.619
Social Stream Ninja, or SSN, is a free,

5
00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:19.765
open-source tool that pulls live chat from YouTube, Twitch,

6
00:00:19.765 --> 00:00:24.100
Kick, TikTok and over a hundred other sites into one dock.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.055
From that dock you can feature a viewer's message on screen,

8
00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:33.750
run polls, giveaways and timers, and drive your overlays in OBS.

9
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.271
SSN runs as a Chrome extension,

10
00:00:37.271 --> 00:00:40.900
or as the standalone desktop app, SSApp.

11
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:45.396
The Stream Deck plugin puts all of that on physical buttons.

12
00:00:45.396 --> 00:00:48.072
There are seventy-seven preset commands:

13
00:00:48.072 --> 00:00:51.871
feature the next message, clear the overlay, start the timer,

14
00:00:51.871 --> 00:00:55.225
roll the credits, show a product, and much more.

15
00:00:55.975 --> 00:00:58.034
Every key gets its own icon.

16
00:00:58.034 --> 00:01:00.202
The big symbol is the feature,

17
00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:02.586
and the small badge is the action:

18
00:01:02.586 --> 00:01:05.275
play, pause, next, reset, or clear.

19
00:01:06.025 --> 00:01:07.771
On a Stream Deck Plus,

20
00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:12.138
turn a dial to adjust the stream timer and press it to start or pause.

21
00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.685
Chat Review lets you scroll recent chat, pin a message,

22
00:01:15.685 --> 00:01:17.900
and feature it with a tap.

23
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.710
With the desktop app, you can also start, stop,

24
00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.696
mute and hide your sources,

25
00:01:23.696 --> 00:01:27.650
and fire your own Event Flow workflows with a single press.

26
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.945
Setup only takes a couple of minutes.

27
00:01:30.945 --> 00:01:34.031
First, download the plugin from the setup page,

28
00:01:34.031 --> 00:01:37.800
and open the file to install it in the Stream Deck app.

29
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.770
Next, copy your session ID.

30
00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:44.910
In SSApp, open the Stream Deck Setup tab and click Copy ID.

31
00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:49.000
With the Chrome extension, you'll find it in Settings.

32
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:53.366
In the Stream Deck app, drag the Setup action onto a key.

33
00:01:53.366 --> 00:01:56.928
Paste your session ID, add your password if you use one,

34
00:01:56.928 --> 00:01:59.175
and choose Test Connection.

35
00:01:59.925 --> 00:02:02.925
When the key says Online, you're connected.

36
00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:07.600
Now add Preset Command keys and pick what each one does.

37
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.075
Every key shares that one connection,

38
00:02:10.075 --> 00:02:12.800
so there's nothing else to configure.

39
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.003
Keep SSN running while you stream,

40
00:02:16.003 --> 00:02:18.650
and keep your session ID private.

41
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.597
Get the plugin, the full controls guide,

42
00:02:22.597 --> 00:02:26.469
and troubleshooting tips at socialstream.ninja/streamdeck.

43
00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:28.200
Happy streaming!
